# "Exile target card from a graveyard": a permanent on the battlefield is not a card in a graveyard, so Bot1's Mox Jet is refused as
# the target (the refusal) while the Island Bot2 discarded to hand size on turn two is not (the positive control, same ability, same
# mana). One card is exiled, and the Curator, with one type (land) among its exiled cards, is still a 3/3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Keen-Eyed Curator
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Keen-Eyed Curator.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Keen-Eyed Curator.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Battlefield.Keen-Eyed Curator.Activate(Bot2.Graveyard.Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Island
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Keen-Eyed Curator.Power = 3
